{"name":"Le Bon Dijon","hex":"#e4cb6b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Bine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bon"},{"term":"dijon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Dijon mustard, a prepared mustard containing white wine in place of vinegar.","A dark yellow color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dijon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bon","blocks":[{"text":"Bon or Bön, also known as Yungdrung Bon, is the indigenous Tibetan religion which shares many similarities and influences with Tibetan Buddhism but retains elements from earlier Tibetan religious traditions. Bon is a significant minority religion in Tibet, especially in the east, as well as in the surrounding Himalayan regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Narshi_Gonpa_Ngawa_Sichuan_China.jpg/330px-Narshi_Gonpa_Ngawa_Sichuan_China.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bon","wikidata":"Q815628"},{"title":"Dijon","blocks":[{"text":"Dijon is a city and the prefecture of the Côte-d'Or department of the Bourgogne-Franche-Comté region in eastern France. As of 2023, the population of the commune was 161,830, making it the most populous commune in Bourgogne-Franche-Comté."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Dijon_-_Puits_de_Mo%C3%AFse_-_02.jpg/330px-Dijon_-_Puits_de_Mo%C3%AFse_-_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dijon","wikidata":"Q7003"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Tonpa_Shenrab.jpg/330px-Tonpa_Shenrab.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Tonpa_Shenrab.jpg/330px-Tonpa_Shenrab.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia